From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Nicholas <70774+bradn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:03:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Comment the iOS port against upstream's original
 behaviour

Records the findings the port relies on where the code uses them: why
inline images never drew upstream (fragments are found only at paragraph
start), what SafeHTML rejected before and that the attribute leniency
applies to the Mac too, that remote HTML images were .inert, where the
Mac view's map-building and code-copy bodies moved, how UIImage sizing
and alpha detection differ from NSImage, how AppKit semantic colours and
accessibility flags map to UIKit, and which targets build for iOS.
Comments only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
